WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.620
Every extra hour of daytime napping tracked with a 13% higher death risk in 1,338 older adults.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.040
This is Longevity Weekly Episode 9. The science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:19.160
After that nap finding, a Missouri survey on routines and pain, a report on semi-glutide

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.760
and Alzheimer's, and then GLP-1 drugs beyond weight loss.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.560
Scientists at Mass General Brigham and Rush University Medical Center, in a JAMA Network

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.780
work-open paper carried by the news international, watched older adults in the rush memory and

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.960
aging project for as long as 19 years after 10 days on a wrist monitor.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.280
One extra nap a day lined up with a 7% higher chance of dying.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.240
Morning naps lined up with a 30% higher mortality risk than afternoon naps.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.320
Irregular schedules did not.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:56.020
Chen Lu Gao read heavy daytime sleep as a possible sign of illness, a chronic condition, broken

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:02.100
night's sleep, or a body clock out of step. The team called it a link, not a cause, and said

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:07.871
more work has to come before those wrist patterns are clinically useful. Yunjin Tracey at the

00:01:07.871 --> 00:01:14.471
University of Missouri, reported by journal Arta, surveyed 67 older adults and did not test whether

00:01:14.471 --> 00:01:21.291
a steadier day treats anything. 37 of them reported in Somnia, and that group also reported more pain

00:01:21.291 --> 00:01:26.611
and more depression. People who woke, ate, saw others, and went to bed at more consistent

00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:31.911
times tended to report less physical pain and fewer depressive symptoms, and poor sleep

00:01:31.911 --> 00:01:36.951
did not wipe the pattern out. Tracy's own line was that, regardless of sleep quality,

00:01:37.451 --> 00:01:42.891
a regular daily routine went with lower pain and less depression than no routine. The National

00:01:42.891 --> 00:01:51.231
Council on Aging says roughly half of adults 60 and older report insomnia symptoms. The

00:01:51.231 --> 00:01:55.591
social jet lag between work days and days off as one possible explanation.

00:01:56.526 --> 00:02:01.446
What is new against the November 11th discussion of these drugs is a science daily report that

00:02:01.446 --> 00:02:05.006
major trials found semi-glutide did not slow Alzheimer's disease.

00:02:05.786 --> 00:02:11.386
Other studies have linked GLP1 medications to a lower risk of dementia, which is an association

00:02:11.386 --> 00:02:12.826
not that trial result.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:18.846
Scientists suspect any memory effect may matter more in obesity or diabetes and before thinking

00:02:18.846 --> 00:02:19.866
problems show up.

00:02:19.866 --> 00:02:22.986
That suspicion is not a trial finding in the report.

00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:26.746
Ozempik and Munjaro are named there as weight loss drugs.

00:02:27.681 --> 00:02:33.901
Partial reprogramming in a preprint lifespan.io describes was tested in three human cell types

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:37.721
and a younger epigenetic age did not always arrive with better function.

00:02:38.341 --> 00:02:43.401
That is a cell study, not a trial in people, and not a product this report puts on a shelf.

00:02:44.021 --> 00:02:49.101
Mount Sinai Hospital in New York in a LinkedIn post is launching a trial rather than publishing

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:55.121
of finished human result. The plan pairs exercise with rapamycin, which the post calls an

00:02:55.121 --> 00:03:00.901
anti-fungal drug, and with spermidine, which it calls a supplement. The available text breaks

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:06.561
off before the endpoints are named. Whether any regulator has approved rapamycin or spermidine

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:13.125
for an aging-related use is not established in that post. Glucagon-like peptide-1 is a gut hormone

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:18.445
released at a meal, and this week's mechanism is what outcome trials show beyond the weight those

00:03:18.445 --> 00:03:24.925
drugs are known for. A 2017 review in Nature Review's Nephrology calls it an Inquiton.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:30.445
It acts on pancreatic eyelid cells, on how much a person eats, and on how the gut moves.

00:03:31.045 --> 00:03:36.745
Those insulin-releasing actions are weaker in type 2 diabetes, which is why GLP1 receptor

00:03:36.745 --> 00:03:42.405
agonists and DPP4 inhibitors were built to treat high blood sugar. The review also sketches

00:03:42.405 --> 00:03:48.325
a gut kidney axis, a fast loop that may handle fluid and salts after eating. As a reason

00:03:48.325 --> 00:03:54.225
to look for a direct kidney effect. The strongest evidence is pooled randomized trials against placebo.

00:03:54.765 --> 00:04:03.545
A 2024 meta-analysis in the Lancet Diabetes and Endocrinology put together 11 trials and 85,373

00:04:03.545 --> 00:04:14.625
people, 29,386 of them women, and 55,987 men. In the 67,769 who had type 2 diabetes,

00:04:14.625 --> 00:04:21.365
disease, the drugs cut a composite kidney outcome by 18%, hazard ratio 0.82%.

00:04:21.365 --> 00:04:26.785
That composite meant kidney failure, a sustained filtration rate drop of at least half, or

00:04:26.785 --> 00:04:28.005
death from kidney failure.

00:04:28.645 --> 00:04:35.965
Kidney failure alone fell 16%, hazard ratio 0.84, major cardiovascular events, meaning

00:04:35.965 --> 00:04:42.845
cardiovascular death, a non-fatal heart attack, or a non-fatal stroke, fell 13%, hazard ratio

00:04:42.845 --> 00:04:50.965
0.87. Death from any cause fell 12%, hazard ratio 0.88. The authors later added select,

00:04:51.345 --> 00:04:58.785
registered as NCT 35874597. A trial in people with cardiovascular disease and a body

00:04:58.785 --> 00:05:04.925
mass index of 27 or higher, who did not have diabetes. Those percentages are the diabetes

00:05:04.925 --> 00:05:12.565
trial figures. A 2021 pool in the same journal. 8 trials and 60,080 patients with type 2

00:05:12.565 --> 00:05:20.825
diabetes, including amplitude O, put the cardiovascular event reduction at 14%, hazard ratio 0.86.

00:05:21.425 --> 00:05:26.665
That review also defined a kidney composite covering new macroalbuminuria, a doubled

00:05:26.665 --> 00:05:32.405
creatinine or at least a 40% filtration drop, kidney replacement or death from kidney disease.

00:05:32.405 --> 00:05:44.125
Its registration is Prospero CRD-42021259711, a 2019 pool, 7 trials and 56,000 4 participants

00:05:44.265 --> 00:05:49.445
cut major cardiovascular events by 12% hazard ratio 0.88.

00:05:50.165 --> 00:05:57.545
The trials were ELI-XA for Lixacenetide, leader for Lyroglutide, sustained 6 for Semaglutide,

00:05:57.545 --> 00:06:04.545
Excell for Exynatide, Harmony Outcomes for Albuglutide, Rewind for Dula Glutide, and

00:06:04.545 --> 00:06:06.725
Pioneer 6 for Oral Semaglutide.

00:06:07.165 --> 00:06:12.505
The abstract says the drugs have beneficial effects on cardiovascular, mortality, and kidney

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:14.245
outcomes in type 2 diabetes.

00:06:15.045 --> 00:06:17.365
Observational comparisons are a lower rung.

00:06:17.905 --> 00:06:26.945
An Eastern China database, 2018 through 2024, held 105,391 people starting a GLP-1 receptor

00:06:26.945 --> 00:06:33.285
agonist or another diabetes drug. After waiting and in both intention to treat and per protocol models,

00:06:33.805 --> 00:06:39.365
other drugs lined up with higher rates than the GLP-1 drugs. Cardiovascular hazard ratios

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:47.685
were 1.19 for SGLT-2 inhibitors, 1.42 for insolence, 1.30 for sulfone ureas,

00:06:47.965 --> 00:06:55.905
and 1.45 for alpha glucosidase inhibitors. Kidney event ratios were 3.09 for DPP-4 inhibitors,

00:06:55.905 --> 00:07:00.685
6.11 for insolence, and 4.56 for megalitonides.

00:07:01.165 --> 00:07:10.285
Liver event ratios were 1.48 for DPP-4 inhibitors, 2.06 for insolence, 1.55 for alpha-glucosidase

00:07:10.285 --> 00:07:13.465
inhibitors, and 1.43 for megalitonides.

00:07:13.685 --> 00:07:17.125
That is an adjusted association, not a randomized proof.

00:07:17.705 --> 00:07:22.665
A U.S. market scan emulation looked at adults with fatty liver disease of the metabolic type

00:07:22.665 --> 00:07:29.305
plus Type-2 diabetes, comparing a GLP-1 drug plus an SGLT-2 inhibitor with either drug

00:07:29.305 --> 00:07:29.565
alone.

00:07:30.085 --> 00:07:37.425
Against the GLP-1 drug alone, 4,606 combination patients were matched to 18,424.

00:07:38.125 --> 00:07:45.885
Over a median 6.3 months, liver events were 39% lower, hazard ratio 0.61, and cardiovascular

00:07:46.345 --> 00:07:50.105
events 35% lower, hazard ratio 0.65.

00:07:50.105 --> 00:07:50.365
5.

00:07:50.845 --> 00:07:58.045
Against the SGLT-2 inhibitor alone, 5368 were matched to 21,472.

00:07:58.645 --> 00:08:05.845
Over a median six months, liver risk was 43% lower, hazard ratio 0.57, and cardiovascular

00:08:05.845 --> 00:08:09.905
risk 20% lower, hazard ratio 0.80.

00:08:10.705 --> 00:08:14.705
Claims data and a few months of follow-up are not a multi-year placebo trial.

00:08:15.205 --> 00:08:19.445
None of these abstracts show the heart or kidney differences standing apart from weight loss.

00:08:19.445 --> 00:08:25.585
None enrolled people to test frailty, biological age, or lifespan. A clinician's choice

00:08:25.585 --> 00:08:30.785
of drug can still shape a drug versus drug comparison. These papers describe the agonists

00:08:30.785 --> 00:08:35.645
as treatments for high blood sugar in type 2 diabetes, and popular reporting also call

00:08:35.645 --> 00:08:41.145
some of them weight loss drugs. Approval to slow aging is not established here. Select is

00:08:41.145 --> 00:08:46.125
the registered human trial added to the 2024 pool. The limit on the strongest finding

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:52.225
is plain, an 18% kidney reduction and a 13% cardiovascular reduction versus placebo

00:08:52.645 --> 00:08:58.045
come from randomized trials and type 2 diabetes, not from a trial of aging, and they do not

00:08:58.045 --> 00:09:00.045
separate any effect from weight change.

00:09:01.045 --> 00:09:05.445
One thing worth knowing is that longer or more frequent daytime naps can mark declining

00:09:05.445 --> 00:09:10.045
health in an observational study without the naps having been shown to cause death.

00:09:10.605 --> 00:09:15.925
A small survey linking steadier days to less pain and fewer depressive symptoms, even when

00:09:15.925 --> 00:09:19.245
When sleep was poor, is an association, not a treatment result.

00:09:19.885 --> 00:09:24.685
Major trials that failed to show somagglutide slowing Alzheimer's are not the same evidence

00:09:24.685 --> 00:09:28.805
as a reported link between GLP-1 drugs and lower dementia risk.

00:09:29.325 --> 00:09:32.045
And fewer heart, kidney, and death events than placebo.

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:37.945
In randomized trials of type 2 diabetes, is a disease outcome record, not a demonstrated

00:09:37.945 --> 00:09:38.905
treatment for aging.

00:09:39.425 --> 00:09:40.665
That's longevity weekly.

00:09:41.065 --> 00:09:43.285
This show is education, not medical advice.

00:09:43.285 --> 00:09:46.845
Talk to your own clinician before acting on anything you heard.

00:09:47.125 --> 00:09:48.505
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:09:48.905 --> 00:09:49.545
See you next week.

